                <pb facs="0607" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg575"/>

                <head>327. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Lebanon<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d327-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-09-20T14:16:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                                1958—2:16 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1307. Embtel 1627.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d327-f2"/> Principally because of need to
                    coordinate US withdrawal from Lebanon with UK withdrawal from Jordan we have
                    come to conclusion date of October 15, which was selected as tentative one for
                    contingency planning purposes, is too early for completion US withdrawal from
                    Lebanon. End of October is more realistic target.</p>
                <p>We have informed Defense of above view, and it has been agreed no operations will
                    now be undertaken based on October 15 as target date for completion. However,
                    routine loading of heavy equipment from Lebanon will continue, and shipping will
                    be unobtrusively gathered together for use in withdrawal operation with possible
                    termination toward end of October, should this time be decided upon.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile we are discussing with UK here coordination re US and UK withdrawals,
                    and hope soon to have an agreed proposed schedule.</p>
                <p>We are also working on a draft US-Lebanese communiqué on US withdrawal from
                    Lebanon which we will send to you for comment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
